BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Calendar-4-1-scaled.webp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/07/Calendar-4-1-scaled.webp
UID:x9g5yaf0kkuG1F8XhfHO8
SUMMARY:EP University: Project Delivery
DTSTAMP:20260817T033540Z
DTSTART:20260819T113000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the third session of the EP University Lecture Seri
	es: Project Delivery. \nAll architecture projects have fundamentally follo
	wed the same processes from programming\, to design\, to documentation and
	 construction. This course reveals the step-by-step process in delivering 
	a project from conception to reality. \n\nReview the phases of design – Pr
	ogramming\, Site Planning\, Schematic Design\, and Design Development – to
	 understand the processes and deliverables for each phase\nUnderstand the 
	project team member roles – internal and external – and how projects move 
	from person to person and phase to phase\nUnderstand the process of develo
	ping construction documents to execute the design vision – from cartoon se
	t\, to establishing what to draw\, why to draw it\, and what team members 
	are responsible for confirming constructability and details\nReview the pr
	ocess of formally issuing drawings including sealing documents\, labelling
	 drawings\, permitting documents\, transmitting drawings and handling draw
	ing revisions\n\nPresented by Jeanette Shaw of Powers Brown Architecture\,
	 this session offers 1LU CE credit.  \nLunch is provided. \nLocation: Powe
	rs Brown Architecture\, MKT 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Suite 300\, Hous
	ton\, TX 77007 \nAdvanced registration is required. Deadline: Monday\, Aug
	ust 17 at 5PM.\n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/ep-university-proj
	ect-delivery/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/ep-university-project-delivery/
LOCATION:Powers Brown Architecture\, MKT 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Suit
	e 300\, Houston\, TX 77007\, 600 N Shepherd\, Building 3\, Ste 300\, Houst
	on\, TX\, 77007
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Concrete-Cosmos.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/05/Concrete-Cosmos.jpg
UID:OGt-4vPCsUKVeQa-TVMjY
SUMMARY:Concrete Cosmos: Composing Skate Architecture
DTSTAMP:20260817T033540Z
DTSTART:20260819T120000Z
DESCRIPTION:In Concrete Cosmos: Composing Skate Architecture\, Shane Yee pr
	esents skate architecture qua architecture\, framing the skatepark as a pa
	radigmatic yet unacknowledged achievement of the contemporary moment\, cha
	racterized by adaptive reuse\, the blurring of public and private space\, 
	an emphasis on lifestyle recreation\, and the ascent of subcultural practi
	ces into mainstream culture. Skate spaces manifest in fluid\, naturalistic
	 configurations\, converging with land art and anticipating parametric/ di
	gital aesthetics\; yet despite this sophistication\, the language and prin
	ciples of the discipline remain largely unarticulated. \nDrawing on a half
	-century history of skatepark design (1976-2026) and his own work at Skate
	 Ecosystems\, Yee offers a chronological series of architectural close rea
	dings\, examining design intentions\, ordering logics\, and formal arrange
	ments. The lecture establishes skate architecture as an emergent field wit
	h significant cultural\, spatial\, and spiritual implications\, capable of
	 producing elevated human experiences. \n\nAbout Shane Yee \nShane Yee ear
	ned his Bachelor of Architecture degree from NewSchool of Architecture & D
	esign in San Diego\, California. Mr. Yee has a broad range of experiences 
	and capabilities in all phases of project planning\, design and constructi
	on- from acquisition through operations and maintenance. He has designed a
	ward-winning projects including residential\, multifamily\, civic\, religi
	ous\, master planning\, and of course\, skate spaces. As an officer in the
	 United States Navy Civil Engineer Corps\, Mr. Yee expertly designed & man
	aged DOD projects with a total value of 100+ million to include Design-Bui
	ld\, DBB\, and MILCON construction. Mr. Yee is a member of the American In
	stitute of Architects\, Society of American Military Engineers\, and US Gr
	een Building Council. \n  \nThis program is in conjunction with Kinetics o
	f Urban Movement\, on view at the Architecture Center Houston from June 18
	-September 26. \nExhibition Sponsors and Community Partners \nKinetics of 
	Urban Movement is funded in part by the City of Houston through Houston Ar
	ts Alliance \n \nCherries Wheels\nHoney Skate Club\nHouston Parks and Recr
	eation Department\nHouston Skate Academy\nSelect\nSkate ECOSYSTEMS\nSouths
	ide Skatepark\n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/concrete-cosmos-com
	posing-skate-architecture/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/concrete-cosmos-composing-skate-a
	rchitecture/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
