UID:4CErhiIoAJ5f1f8RVyofs
SUMMARY:People of Hope Traveling Museum at Mamie George Community Center
DTSTAMP:20260817T033540Z
DTSTART:20260911T120000Z
DESCRIPTION:Catholic Charities of the Archdiocese of Galveston-Houston welc
	omes the People of Hope Traveling Museum\, an immersive storytelling exper
	ience\, at Mamie George Community Center in Richmond. \nThe exhibit highli
	ghts stories of poverty\, service\, and hope. \nGuests will learn how pove
	rty affects vulnerable populations—including children\, seniors\, and vete
	rans. \nThey’ll also hear firsthand accounts of what it means to serve peo
	ple in their darkest hour\, including a story from a staff member at the C
	atholic Charities of the Archdiocese of Galveston-Houston. \nPeople of Hop
	e is on a nationwide tour\, celebrating the power and transformative impac
	t of service to others. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more. \n \nThis Featured 
	Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our c
	alendar with images and more details. \nLearn more about promoting your ev
	ent\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.\n\nht
	tps://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/people-of-hope-traveling-museum-at-m
	amie-george-community-center/\n\nFrom 365 Things to Do in Houston
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/people-of-hope-traveling-museum
	-at-mamie-george-community-center/
LOCATION:Mamie George Community Center\, 1111 Collins Rd\, Richmond\, Richm
	ond\, 77469\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:365-things-houston
CATEGORIES:365 Things to Do in Houston
